    pr_ref:  # 6c04
    description: "php.py `_extract_laravel_routes` refuses a route whose path literal is empty (`if not route_path: continue`), so `Route::get('', [HomeController::class, 'index'])` emits neither a UsageContext nor a route marker. Laravel trims slashes from a URI, so '' registers the same route as '/'. The idiom is common inside a prefix group (`Route::prefix('admin')->group(function () { Route::get('', ...); })`).\n\nLive repro (2026-10-01, ~/hg_wt/fadip with WI-fadip's fix): analyze_php on `Route::get('', [HomeController::class, 'index']);` emits 0 contexts and 0 route markers.\n\nSince WI-fadip, `_php_string_value` returns \"\" for an empty literal and None only for a non-literal or interpolated string, so the fix is to test `route_path is None` (refuse) separately from `route_path == \"\"` (normalize to \"/\"). This is ABSENT != EMPTY (LIVE section 5): the empty literal is a positive value, not an absent one.\n\nNot measured: frequency on a corpus.\nFound while fixing WI-fadip-tojup-fonug-hokoz-bomin-jarib-javik-vibud (not a quote-style defect, so filed separately)."  # 6c04
    fields: {}  # 6c04
